<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=basket-weaving">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basket weaving</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 8000 BCE</span> · Also known as Basketry, Basket making</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Basket weaving is the process of weaving or sewing pliable materials such as willow, grasses, vines and splints into baskets, mats and similar objects. Its age is hard to establish because the materials decay. The oldest known baskets, found in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faiyum">Faiyum</a> in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, have been carbon dated to between 10,000 and 12,000 years old, earlier than any established pottery vessels. The oldest and largest complete basket, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negev">Negev</a>, is 10,500 years old. Basketry is often evidenced only by the imprint of a weave on fragments of fired clay pots.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basket-weaving.jpg" alt="Basket weaving" width="330" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ymea · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman_weaving_baskets_near_Lake_Ossa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 10,000 years ago</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Faiyum, Egypt</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Techniques indistinguishable from rope making are evidenced since the earliest hominin presence in South Africa, but no specimens survive.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/rope">Rope<span>c. 24,000 years ago</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=basket-weaving">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
